\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. HOW beauteous are their feet
\par Who stand on Zion's hill,
\par Who bring salvation in their tongues,
\par And words of peace reveal!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How cheering is their voice,
\par How sweet the tidings are!
\par Zion, behold thy Saviour King;
\par He reigns and triumphs here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How blessed are our ears
\par That hear this joyful sound,
\par Which kings and prophets waited for,
\par And sought, but never found.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. How blessed are our eyes 
\par That see this heavenly light,
\par Prophets and kings desired long,
\par But died without the sight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The watchmen join their voice,
\par And tuneful notes employ;
\par Jerusalem breaks forth in songs,
\par And deserts learn the joy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The Lord makes bare His arm
\par Through all the earth abroad:
\par Let all the nations now behold
\par Their Saviour and their God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

